  "detail": "`updateAttempted` latches after the first try and `updateTarget ??=` never changes, so a transient `git fetch` error or lock contention leaves the worker advertising zero slots forever: network recovery, a newer coordinator release, or a coordinator rollback to the worker's own release don't help. Track the latest release the coordinator reports; when it equals the worker's own, clear the update state and take jobs again; when it changes, start over. Retry transient failures with a bounded backoff (one retry layer, a deadline per target), keep the last failure as the warning, and don't retry a permanent validation failure (a SHA not on origin/main) for the same target. Add tests: a transient failure followed by a successful retry; a target change after a failure; a coordinator that returns to the worker's release."
